; DOMAIN: mathematics/algebra/lie-algebra [CLOSED, derived 2026-08-01]; Claim: Lie algebras are vector spaces equipped with a bilinear bracket operation [x,y] satisfying antisymmetry and the Jacobi identity. They arise as tangent spaces of Lie groups at the identity, encoding infinitesimal symmetries. Key concepts include the adjoint representation, Killing form (whose nondegeneracy characterizes semisimplicity by Cartan's criterion), root systems and Dynkin diagrams classifying simple Lie algebras over C (types A_n, B_n, C_n, D_n plus exceptional E_6, E_7, E_8, F_4, G_2), universal enveloping algebra (via PBW theorem), and the Weyl character formula. Applications span particle physics (gauge symmetries), differential geometry (symmetry of manifolds), and representation theory.; Structure: (Lie algebra: vector space with bilinear bracket [x,y]) (antisymmetry: [x,y] = -[y,x]) (Jacobi identity: [x,[y,z]] + [y,[z,x]] + [z,[x,y]] = 0) (adjoint representation: ad_x(y) = [x,y]) (Killing form: B(x,y) = Tr(ad_x ad_y)) (Cartan criterion: semisimple iff Killing form nondegenerate) (root system: weights of Cartan subalgebra action) (Dynkin classification: A_n, B_n, C_n, D_n, E_6, E_7, E_8, F_4, G_2)
; Result: Lie algebras linearize Lie groups by taking tangent spaces at the identity, converting nonlinear group structure into algebraic bracket operations. The Killing form provides an invariant bilinear form whose nondegeneracy (Cartan's criterion) precisely characterizes semisimplicity. Root systems and Dynkin diagrams give a complete classification of simple Lie algebras over C, connecting to reflection groups and crystallographic lattices. The universal enveloping algebra (PBW theorem) provides a bridge to representation theory and quantum groups. The Weyl character formula computes irreducible characters from highest weight data.
; Bridge: genesis_representation_theory + genesis_sylow + genesis_category_theory + genesis_spectral_theorem + genesis_homology + genesis_group_cohomology
;; A Lie algebra is a vector space with a bilinear bracket satisfying antisymmetry and Jacobi identity
(|- ((==> (&& (--> VectorSpace $g) (--> BilinearBracket $bracket) (--> Antisymmetric $bracket) (--> JacobiIdentity $bracket))) (--> LieAlgebra $g)) (stv 1.0 0.9))
(|- ((==> (&& (--> LieAlgebra $g) (--> BilinearMap $ad) (--> Equals ($ad $x $y) (Bracket $x $y)) (--> Homomorphism $ad))) (--> AdjointRepresentation $ad $g)) (stv 1.0 0.9))
;; Killing form B(x,y) = Tr(ad_x circ ad_y) is a symmetric invariant bilinear form
(|- ((==> (&& (--> LieAlgebra $g) (--> BilinearForm $B) (--> Equals ($B $x $y) (Trace (Compose (ad $x) (ad $y)))) (--> Invariant $B))) (--> KillingForm $B $g)) (stv 1.0 0.9))
;; Cartan criterion: semisimple iff Killing form is nondegenerate
(|- ((==> (&& (--> LieAlgebra $g) (--> KillingForm $B $g) (--> Nondegenerate $B))) (--> Semisimple $g)) (stv 1.0 0.9))
;; Root system: weights of Cartan subalgebra action on the Lie algebra
(|- ((==> (&& (--> LieAlgebra $g) (--> CartanSubalgebra $h) (--> Weight $alpha) (--> Eigenspace $g_alpha))) (--> RootSystem $Phi $g $h)) (stv 1.0 0.9))
;; Dynkin classification: simple Lie algebras over C classified by Dynkin diagrams (A_n, B_n, C_n, D_n, E_6, E_7, E_8, F_4, G_2)
(|- ((==> (&& (--> LieAlgebra $g) (--> Simple $g) (--> Field C) (--> DynkinDiagram $D))) (--> DynkinClassification $g $D)) (stv 1.0 0.9))
;; PBW theorem: universal enveloping algebra U(g) is isomorphic to symmetric algebra S(g) as filtered vector spaces
(|- ((==> (&& (--> LieAlgebra $g) (--> UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra $U) (--> SymmetricAlgebra $S) (--> Isomorphism $phi))) (--> PBWTheorem $U $S $phi)) (stv 1.0 0.9))
;; Weyl character formula: irreducible character of highest weight representation
(|- ((==> (&& (--> LieAlgebra $g) (--> Semisimple $g) (--> HighestWeight $lambda) (--> IrreducibleRepresentation $V_lambda) (--> WeylGroup $W))) (--> WeylCharacterFormula (Character $V_lambda) (WeylDenominator $lambda) (WeylNumerator $lambda))) (stv 1.0 0.9))
